From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:14:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tolerate a sub-cell width change instead of re-breaking

Under a cell grid, rounding runs after the line break and rounds a
box's left and right edges independently, so a container nothing
touched still commits a width up to one cell from the width its lines
were broken at. The clobber check compared with a half-pixel tolerance,
so it declared every inline root on such a page stale and re-broke it
through parley's break_all_lines, which knows nothing about floats.
A floated infobox therefore stopped shortening any line box: on
Wikipedia in the terminal grid modes the article text ran
straight underneath the infobox, and the words it covered were simply
gone from the page.

Tolerating a sub-cell difference costs no correction, because on a grid
where every glyph is one cell wide a width change smaller than a cell
cannot move a break. The half-pixel tolerance stays wherever the grid
is off.
---
 src/resolve.rs | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/resolve.rs b/src/resolve.rs
index f332ecc..cf0d2aa 100644
--- a/src/resolve.rs
+++ b/src/resolve.rs
@@ -784,6 +784,9 @@ impl BaseDocument {
         if skip && !cfg!(debug_assertions) {
             return;
         }
+        // Rounding runs after line breaking and rounds both box edges.
+        // On a cell grid, a sub-cell width change cannot move a glyph.
+        let width_tol = self.round_grid.0.max(0.5);
         let mut stale: Vec<(NodeId, f32)> = Vec::new();
         let mut roots = std::mem::take(&mut self.inline_roots);
         // Only the push sites can add duplicates or unsorted ids; if none ran
@@ -819,7 +822,7 @@ impl BaseDocument {
                 l.size.width - l.padding.left - l.padding.right - l.border.left - l.border.right;
             if content_w > 0.0 {
                 let unbroken = !inline.last_break_width.is_finite();
-                if unbroken || (content_w - inline.last_break_width).abs() > 0.5 {
+                if unbroken || (content_w - inline.last_break_width).abs() > width_tol {
                     stale.push((id, content_w));
                 }
             }
